.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_CLONE 3 2026-08-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_clone \- clone an MPQ archive for independent reading.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_clone("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "clone",
.BI "        mpq_archive_s  *" "source"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Call \fBlibmpq__archive_clone\fP() to reopen the backing path of an archive
with an independent file stream, decoded metadata tables, and lazy block
caches. A source handle may be closed after cloning succeeds, and each
clone must be closed independently with \fBlibmpq__archive_close\fP().
.PP
Cloning is independent-handle support, not snapshot semantics. The original
path must remain readable and unchanged while clones are created or used.
The source handle itself remains unsafe for concurrent operations; create one
clone per worker instead.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, *\fIclone\fP is set to a new handle and zero is returned. On
failure, *\fIclone\fP is set to NULL and the open, seek, read, format, or
allocation error is returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_open (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
